  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_avg_pool_2d(image: list, pool_size: int = 2) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Average Pool 2D** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_avg_pool_2d(image: list, pool_size: int = 2) -> list:\n    img = np.array(image, dtype=float)\n    oh, ow = img.shape[0] // pool_size, img.shape[1] // pool_size\n    out = np.zeros((oh, ow))\n    for i in range(oh):\n        for j in range(ow): out[i, j] = np.mean(img[i*pool_size:(i+1)*pool_size, j*pool_size:(j+1)*pool_size])\n    return np.round(out, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
